          %h3#LocalTopos Local topos
          #local.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
              is a
              %strong local topos
              if the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒯
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mi Γ
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi LConst
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T} \stackrel{\overset{LConst}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{\Gamma}{\to}} Set
              has a further
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi CoDisc
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CoDisc
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi LConst
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi CoDisc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (LConst \dashv \Gamma \dashv CoDisc)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CoDisc
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Set
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi 𝒯
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    CoDisc \colon Set \hookrightarrow \mathcal{T}.
            %p
              (As just stated, it is automatic in the case over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
              that this is furthermore a
              = succeed ".)" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Another way of stating this is that a Grothendieck topos is local if and only if the terminal object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+object"} connected
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+object"} projective
              (since this means precisely that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo =
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma = \hom(1, -)
              preserves colimits, and therefore has a right adjoint by virtue of an
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor+theorem"} adjoint functor theorem
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              is
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tiny+object"} tiny
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atomic+object"}> atomic
              ). Notice the similarity to the concept of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/amazing+right+adjoint"} amazing right adjoint
              (the difference being that this is a right adjoint not to the external but to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
              out of 1.)
          %p
            Note also that in an infinitary-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensive+category"} extensive category
            an object is connected as soon as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom(X,-)
            preserves
            %em binary
            coproducts (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+object"} connected object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom(1,-)
            preserves binary coproducts and epis. Moreover, a cospan
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo ←
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to C \leftarrow B
            in a topos is a coproduct diagram iff
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            are disjoint monos whose union is all of
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom(1,-)
            preserves binary coproducts as soon as it preserves the initial object and binary unions. This leads to the following equivalent form of “locality” that makes sense even for elementary toposes:
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              An
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+topos"} elementary topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              is
              %em local
              if the terminal object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              is
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  nonempty:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ≇
                          %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\ncong 0
              %li
                %p
                  connected:
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo =
                        %mi p
                        %mo ∨
                        %mi q
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 = p \vee q
                  implies
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo =
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 = p
                  or
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo =
                          %mi q
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 = q
              %li
                %p
                  projective: every epi
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo →
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \to 1
                  admits a section
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi t
                          %mo :
                          %mn 1
                          %mo →
                          %mi U
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t: 1 \to U
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              Some authors have instead used the term “local” to refer just to the condition that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              is connected; note this is equivalent to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sub
                      %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub_E(1)
              being a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+ring"} local rig
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#Awodey"} thesis
              %em hyperlocal
              if both connectivity and projectivity are satisfied. As argued above, for a Grothendieck topos this is slightly
              %em weaker
              than locality, although the difference is only in the inclusion of the trivial topos (for if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ≅
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\cong 0
              then
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo ≃
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E\simeq 1
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-pointed+topos"} constructively well-pointed
              if and only if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              is additionally a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generator"} generator
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+topos"} free topos
              is a local elementary topos.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#EquivalentCharacterizations Equivalent characterizations
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              A geometric morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : E \to S
              is local precisely if
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  there exists a geometric morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo :
                        %mi S
                        %mo →
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c : S \to E
                  such that
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo ∘
                          %mi c
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi id
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \circ c \simeq id
              %li
                %p
                  for every other geometric morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo :
                        %mi G
                        %mo →
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g : G \to S
                  the composite
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi g
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c\circ g
                  is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
                  in the hom-category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Topos
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo ,
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Topos_{/S}(g,f)
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Topos"} Topos
                  over
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#Johnstone"}> Johnstone, theorem 3.6.1 vi)
            ).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              In particular this means that the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+points"} topos points
              of a local topos has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible"} contractible
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
          %h3#general General
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
              geometric morphism of any local
              = succeed "-topos" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒮
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+topos"} base topos
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒮
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+fibration"} Grothendieck fibration
              and a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+opfibration"} Grothendieck opfibration
          %p
            This appears in (
            %a{:href => "#Shulman"}> Shulman
            ).
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Freyd+cover"} Freyd cover
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+topos"} local topos
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract"} retract
              of a Freyd cover.
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#Johnstone"}> Johnstone, lemma C3.6.4
            ).
          %h3#HomotopyDimension Homotopy dimension
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              In a local
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
              over
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+object"} inhabited object
              is globally inhabited:
            %p
              every object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              for which the unique morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to *
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+point"} global point
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} * \to X
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Since in a local topos the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
              functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphisms"} epimorphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(X) \to \Gamma(*) \simeq *
              is an epimorphism in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjection"} surjection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(X)
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited"} inhabited
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(X) \simeq Hom(*,X)
              (see
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section+geometric+morphism"} global section geometric morphism
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              In a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
              every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+epimorphism"} effective epimorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to *
              being an epi means that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28-1%29-connected"} (-1)-connected
              object. Therefore the above statement says in terms of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category+theory"} (infinity,1)-category theory
              that a non-trivial local topos has
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+dimension"} homotopy dimension
              0.
            %p
              The same is true for any
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} local (infinity,1)-topos
          %h3#concrete_sheaves Concrete sheaves
          %p
            Every local topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma : E \to S
            comes with a notion of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+sheaves"} concrete sheaves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Conc
                    %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Conc_\Gamma(E) \hookrightarrow E
            which factors the topos inclusion of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi Codisc
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi Γ
                  %msub
                    %mi Conc
                    %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi Conc
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S
                  \\stackrel{\overset{\Gamma}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{Codisc}{\hookrightarrow}}
                  Conc_\Gamma(E)
                  \\stackrel{\overset{Conc}{\leftarrow}}{\hookrightarrow}
                  E
          %p
            and is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasitopos"} quasitopos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+sheaf"} concrete sheaf
            for details.
          %h3#homotopy_equivalence Homotopy equivalence
          %p
            Since a local geometric morphism has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Topos"} Topos
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence+of+toposes"} homotopy equivalence of toposes
          %h2#ElementaryAxiomatization Elementary Axiomatization
          %p
            For any local topos
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \colon \mathcal{E} \to \mathcal{S}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒮
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
            is equivalent to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} category of sheaves
            for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere-Tierney+topology"} Lawvere-Tierney topology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiomatization"} axiomatization
            of local maps of (bounded) toposes can be given in terms of properties of topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            and topology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            (
            %a{:href => "#AwodeyBirkedal"}> AwodeyBirkedal
            )
          %p We discuss first
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#SetupForAxiomatization"} the setup
          %p and then
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#TheAxioms"} the axioms
          %p themselves.
          %h3#SetupForAxiomatization The setup
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+topos"} elementary topos
            equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere-Tierney+topology"} Lawvere-Tierney topology
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo :
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j : \Omega \to \Omega
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo ♯
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \mapsto \sharp  V
            for the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closure+operation"} closure operation
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \hookrightarrow X
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sharp+modality"} sharp modality
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi V
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo ♯
                          %mi V
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi χ
                                %mi V
                        %mtd
                          %mi Ω
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi j
                        %mtd
                          %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  V &amp;\to&amp; {*}
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\sharp  V &amp;\to&amp; &amp;\to&amp; {*}
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow  &amp;&amp;  \downarrow
                  \\\
                  X &amp;\stackrel{\chi_V}{\to}&amp; \Omega
                  \&amp;\stackrel{j}{\to}&amp;
                  \\Omega
                  }
          %p Write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi coDisc
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo →
                      %mi coDisc
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi Γ
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\Gamma \dashv coDisc)
                  \:
                  Sh_j(\mathcal{E})
                  \\stackrel{\overset{\Gamma}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{coDisc}{\to}}
                  \\mathcal{E}
          %p
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} of j-sheaves
          #EssentialTopology.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              We say that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              is an
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+geometric+morphism"} essential
                topology
              if for all objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              the closure operation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♯
                    %mo :
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sharp  : Sub(X) \to Sub(X)
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/posets+of+subobjects"} posets of subobjects
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ♭
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mo ♯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat \dashv \sharp
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ↪
                    %mo ♯
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ♭
                    %mi U
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (U \hookrightarrow \sharp  V)
                    \\Leftrightarrow
                    (\flat U \hookrightarrow V)
                    \\,.
          %p
            This appears under the term “principal” in (
            %a{:href => "#AwodeyBirkedal"}> Awodey-Birkedal, def. 2.1
            ).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_5 Remark
            %p
              We use the notation “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♭
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat
              ” and “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sharp
              ” oppositely to the use on p.14 of
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#AwodeyBirkedal"} Awodey-Birkedal
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+topos"} cohesive topos
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (infinity,1)-topos
              = succeed "\u201D" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ♭
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat
          .num_observation
            %h6#observation Observation
            %p
              The left adjoints
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♭
                    %mo :
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat : Sub(X) \to Sub(X)
              for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathcal{E}
              extend to a functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♭
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat : \mathcal{E} \to \mathcal{E}
              on all of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p (…)
          #InternalCharacterizationOfLocalReflection.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere-Tierney+topology"} Lawvere-Tierney topology
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#EssentialTopology"} essential
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo ♭
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mo ♯
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\flat \dashv \sharp )
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              there exists a least
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ♯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sharp
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+subobject"} dense subobject
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi X
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_X \hookrightarrow X
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#AwodeyBirkedal"}> AwodeyBirkedal, lemma 2.3
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              By the discussion at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} category of sheaves
              we have that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sharp
              is given by the composite
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♯
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi Γ
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi coDisc
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\sharp  : \mathcal{E} \stackrel{\Gamma}{\to} Sh_j(\mathcal{E}) \stackrel{coDisc}{\hookrightarrow} \mathcal{E}
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the first morphism is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheafification"} sheafification
              and the second is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful
            %p
              If now the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♭
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat
              exists, it follows that this comes from a left adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Disc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Disc
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♭
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mi Γ
                      %mover
                        %mo ↩
                        %mi Disc
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi coDisc
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi Γ
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo :
                    %mo ♯
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\flat
                    \:
                    \\mathcal{E}
                    \\stackrel{\overset{Disc}{\hookleftarrow}}{\underset{\Gamma}
                    {\to}}
                    Sh_j(\mathcal{E})
                    \\stackrel{\overset{\Gamma}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{coDisc}{\hookrightarrow}}
                    \\mathcal{E}
                    \:
                    \\sharp
                    \\,.
            %p
              Therefore the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Disc
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Disc \dashv \Gamma)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit+of+an+adjunction"} counit
              provides morphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ♭
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ♭
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\flat X \to X) = (\flat X \to U_x \hookrightarrow X)
                    \\,,
            %p
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
              factorization
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x \hookrightarrow X
              we claim provides the least dense subobjects.
            %p
              To show that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_X
              is dense it is sufficient to show that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ♭
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi coDisc
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi Disc
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo →
                    %mi coDisc
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\sharp (\flat X \to X)
                    \=
                    (coDisc \Gamma Disc \Gamma \to coDisc \Gamma X)
            %p
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %p
              Composing this morphism with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CoDisc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CoDisc
              of the
              = succeed "-unit" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Disc
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Disc \dashv\Gamma)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma X
              (which is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Disc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Disc
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
              by the discussion at
              = succeed ")" do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "adjoint+triple#FullyFaithFulAdjointTriples"} fully faithful adjoint triples
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Disc
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Disc \dashv \Gamma)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangle+identity"} triangle identity
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi coDisc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi Disc
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi coDisc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi Id
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    coDisc(
                    \\Gamma X
                    \\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                    \\Gamma Disc \Gamma X
                    \\stackrel{}{\to}
                    \\Gamma X
                    )
                    \=
                    coDisc ( \Gamma X \stackrel{Id}{\to} \Gamma X)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Using that also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi coDisc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} coDisc
              is full and faithful and then
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-out-of-3"} 2-out-of-3
              for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
              it follows that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi coDisc
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi Disc
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi coDisc
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} coDisc \Gamma Disc \Gamma X \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} coDisc \Gamma X
              hence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♯
                    %mo ♭
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mo ♯
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\sharp  \flat X \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} \sharp  X
            %p is indeed an isomorphism.
            %p
              Moreover, by one of the equivalent characterizations of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategories"} reflective subcategories
              we have (…)
          #DiscreteObjects.num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              An object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathcal{E}
              is called
              %strong discrete
              if for all
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+isomorphisms"} local isomorphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : A \to B
              the induced morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{E}(X,A) \to \mathcal{E}(X,B)
            %p
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              (of sets, hence a bijection).
          #ODiscreteObjects.num_defn
            %h6#definition_7 Definition
            %p
              An object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathcal{E}
              is called
              %strong o-discrete
              if
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ♭
                      %mi X
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat X \simeq X
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p Every discrete object is o-discrete.
          %h3#the_axioms The axioms
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_8 Definition
            %p
              On
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+topos"} elementary topos
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere-Tierney+topology"} Lawvere-Tierney topology
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              consider the following axioms.
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %strong> Axiom 1
                  \.
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
                  is
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a{:href => "#EssentialTopology"} essential
              %li
                %p
                  %strong> Axiom 2 a
                  \. There is an object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℰ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \in \mathcal{E}
                  such that every object is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subquotient"} subquotient
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
                  of a
                  %a{:href => "#DiscreteObjects"} discrete object
                  with
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %li
                %p
                  %strong> Axiom 2 b
                  \. With
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  as above, there is a discrete object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G'
                  and an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                          %mo ′
                          %mo →
                          %mo ♭
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G' \to \flat G
              %li
                %p
                  %strong> Axiom 3
                  \. For all
                  %a{:href => "#DiscreteObjects"} discrete objects
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi D
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [X,D]
                  is
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "#ODiscreteObjects"} o-discrete
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  is also discrete.
              %li
                %p
                  %strong> Axiom 4
                  \.
                  %a{:href => "#DiscreteObjects"} Discrete objects
                  are closed under binary
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              These axioms characterize local geometric morphisms
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi Sh
                        %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mi D
                        %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E} \to Sh_j(\mathcal{E}) \simeq D_j(\mathcal{E})
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              is fixed to be the terminal object (in which case Axiom 2 b becomes empty), then they characterize local and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localic+geometric+morphisms"} localic geometric morphisms
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#AwodeyBirkedal"}> Awodey-Birkedal, theorem 3.1
            ) together with the discussion around remark 3.7.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#EasyExamples Easy examples
          #PresheafToposOverSiteWithTerminal.num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
              with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} * \in C
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op},Set]
              is a local topos.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              Notice that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set \simeq [*,Set]
              is the presheaf topos over the point category, the category with a single object and a single morphism. Therefore the constant presheaf functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Const
                    %mo :
                    %mi Set
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Const : Set \to [C^{op}, Set]
            %p
              can be thought of as sending a set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in Set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo :
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S : * \to Set
              to the composite functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Const
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi S
                    %mi Set
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Const(S) \colon C \to * \stackrel{S}{\to} Set
                    \\,.
            %p
              Notice that in the presence of a terminal object in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Const
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Const
              is a
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Const
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Const
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Const(S_1) \to Const(S_2)
              has components
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi S
                              %mn 1
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi Const
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi S
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi Const
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi S
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi S
                              %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi Const
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi S
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Const
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi S
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    S_1 = &amp; Const(S_1)(*) &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; Const(S_2)(*) &amp; = S_2
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrm{id}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrm{id}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; Const(S_1)(U) &amp;\to&amp; Const(S_2)(U)
                    }
            %p
              where the vertical morphisms are
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Const
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo →
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Const(U \to *)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in C
              given the presence of the terminal object. It follows that such a natural transformation is given by any and one and the same
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon S_1 \to S_2
            %p
              The functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Const
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Const
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              and a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
              operations
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi Const
                    %mo ⊢
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo ←
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\underset{\rightarrow}{\lim} \vdash Const \vdash \underset{\leftarrow}{\lim})
            %p
              which send a presheaf/functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon C^{op} \to Set
              to its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{\rightarrow}{\lim} F \in Set
              or
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo ←
                      %mi F
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{\leftarrow}{\lim} F \in Set
            %p
              Since adjoints are essentially unique, it follows that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
              functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \colon [C^{op}, Set]
              is given by taking the limit,
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ≃
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo ←
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \simeq \underset{\leftarrow}{\lim}
            %p
              Observe that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} * \in C
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              with initial object is given simply by evaluation at that object, and so we have for any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \in [C^{op}, Set]
              that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Γ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %mo ←
                            %mi F
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\Gamma(F) &amp; \simeq \underset{\leftarrow}{\lim} F
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq F(*) \in Set
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              hence that the global section functor is simply given by evaluating a presheaf on the terminal object of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %p
              Limits and colimit
              %em in
              a presheaf category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op}, Set]
              are computed objectwise over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              (see at
              = succeed ")." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits+and+colimits+by+example"} limits and colimits by example
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              preserves in limits and colimits, and in particular evaluation at the terminal object does. Therefore
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              preserves all colimits. Hence by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor+theorem"} adjoint functor theorem
              it has a further
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi CoDisc
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CoDisc
            %p
              We can compute it explicitly by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              and using the defining Hom-isomorphism of adjoints to be the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CoDisc
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Set
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CoDisc \colon Set \to [C^{op}, Set]
              such that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in Set
              the presheaf
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CoDisc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CoDisc(S)
              is given over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in C
              by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi CoDisc
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo →
                              %mi Yoneda
                              %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %msup
                                  %mi C
                                  %mi op
                                %mo ,
                                %mi Set
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo ,
                            %mi CoDisc
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo →
                              %mi adjunction
                              %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi Set
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Γ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    CoDisc(S)(U) &amp; \underoverset{Yoneda}{\simeq}{\to} Hom_{[C^{op}, Set]}(U,CoDisc(S))
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \underoverset{adjunction}{\simeq}{\to} Hom_{Set}(\Gamma(U), S)
                    \\,.
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              So in conclusion we have an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Const
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi CoDisc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Const \vdash \Gamma \vdash CoDisc)
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Const
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Const
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
              %em
                %a{:href => "adjoint+triple#FullyFaithFulAdjointTriples"} fully faithful adjoint triples
              it follows then that also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CoDisc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CoDisc
              is full and faithful.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p
              The converse to prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PresheafToposOverSiteWithTerminal"}
              is true if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+complete+category"} Cauchy complete
          .num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X)
              is local (over Set) iff
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/focal+point"} focal point
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighborhood"} neighborhood
              is the whole space. In this case, the extra right adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo !
                    %mo :
                    %mi Set
                    %mo →
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^! : Set \to Sh(X)
              to the global sections functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_* : Sh(X) \to Set
              is given by the functor which computes the stalk at
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi U
                    %mo =
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ,
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "left left", :displaystyle => "false"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi M
                              %mo ,
                            %mtd
                              %mi U
                              %mo =
                              %mi X
                              %mo ,
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                              %mo ⋆
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                              %mo ,
                            %mtd
                              %mi U
                              %mo ≠
                              %mi X
                              %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma(U, f^!(M)) = Hom(\{\star|U=X\}, M) \cong
                    \\begin{cases} M, &amp; U = X, \\ \{\star\}, &amp; U \neq X, \end{cases}
            %p
              for sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              and open subsets
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subseteq X
          %h3#sheaves_on_a_local_site Sheaves on a local site
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+site"} local site
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} category of sheaves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
            is a local topos over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
          %p
            For instance
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
            is a local site. Objects in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+spaces"} generalized smooth spaces
            such as
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+space"} diffeological space
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Codisc
                  %mo :
                  %mi Set
                  %mo →
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi CartSp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Codisc : Set \to Sh(CartSp)
          %p
            is the functor that sends a set to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+space"} diffeological space
            on that set with
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codiscrete+space"} codiscrete
            smooth structure (every map of sets is smooth).
          %h3#relative_realizability Relative Realizability
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be a partial combinatory algebra and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ♯
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\sharp\subseteq A
            be a sub partial combinatory algebra of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %span.newWikiWord
              relative realizability topos
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/relative+realizability+topos"} ?
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} RT
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo ♯
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{RT}(A,A\sharp)
            to the standard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/realizability+topos"} realizability topos
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} RT
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ♯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{RT}(A\sharp)
          %h3#localization Localization
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi LocTopos
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LocTopos
            denote the 2-category of local
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+toposes"} Grothendieck toposes
            (over Set) with all geometric morphisms between them. Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi PTopos
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PTopos
            denote the 2-category whose objects are
            %span.newWikiWord
              pointed toposes
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/pointed+topos"} ?
            (i.e. (Grothendieck) toposes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            equipped with a geometric morphism
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Set
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\colon Set\to E
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f,\alpha)
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon E\to E'
            is a geometric morphism and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi s
                  %mo ′
                  %mo →
                  %mi f
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha\colon s'\to f s
            is a (not necessarily invertible) geometric transformation.
          %p
            Note that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is a local topos with global sections geometric morphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mo *
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e^*\dashv e_*
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_*\dashv e^!
            is also a geometric morphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set\to E
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi LocTopos
                    %mo →
                    %mi PTopos
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LocTopos \to PTopos
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            %strong localization
            of a pointed topos at its specified point. For example:
          #LocalizationOfPresheafTopos.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_7 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is an object of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op},Set]
              at the point induced by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\colon 1\to C
              can be identified with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi U
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [(C/U)^{op},Set]
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over+category"} over category
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              = succeed "es," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over+topos"} over topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)/U
              (where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is regarded in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)
              by the
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_8 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X=Spec(A)
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zariski+spectrum"} Zariski spectrum
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P\subset A
              is a prime ideal of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              (i.e. a point of
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X)
              at
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P\colon 1\to X
              can be identified with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Spec
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(Spec(A_P))
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_P
              denotes the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              at
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
          %p
            A similar construction is possible for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+geometric+morphism"} bounded
            toposes over any base (not just Set).
          %h3#LocalOverTopoes Local over-toposes
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_9 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathcal{E}
              an object, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over+topos"} over topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}/X
              is local if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tiny+object"} tiny object
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atomic+object"}> atomic object
              ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_5 Proof
            %p
              We check that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma : \mathcal{E}/X \to Set
              preserves
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-functor"} hom-functor
              out of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}/X
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi Id
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X \stackrel{Id}{\to} X)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi f
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℰ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Id
                      %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma : (A \stackrel{f}{\to} X) \mapsto Hom_{\mathcal{E}/X}(Id_X, f)
                    \\,.
            %p
              The
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over+category"} over category
              are
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mrow
                                %mi ℰ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi Id
                              %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo →
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi ℰ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi Id
                                  %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi ℰ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Hom_{\mathcal{E}/X}(Id_X, (A \to X)) &amp;\to&amp;
                    Hom_{\mathcal{E}}(X,A)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{f_*}
                    \\\
                    * &amp;\stackrel{Id_x}{\to}&amp; Hom_{\mathcal{E}}(X,X)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Moreover, overserve that
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over+category"} over category
              are computed in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi i
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {\lim_{\to}}_i (A_i \stackrel{f_i}{\to} X)
                    \\simeq
                    ({\lim_\to}_i A_i) \to X
                    \\,.
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tiny+object"} tiny object
              then by definition we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi lim
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_{\mathcal{E}}(X, {\lim}_i A_i)
                    \\simeq
                    {\lim_\to}_i Hom_{\mathcal{E}}(X, A_i)
                    \\,,
            %p Inserting all this into the above pullback gives the pullback
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mrow
                                %mi ℰ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi Id
                              %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                                %munder
                                  %mi lim
                                  %mo →
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi i
                            %mo →
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                                %munder
                                  %mi lim
                                  %mo →
                              %mi i
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi ℰ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi Id
                                  %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi ℰ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Hom_{\mathcal{E}/X}(Id_X, {\lim_\to}_i (A_i \to X)) &amp;\to&amp;
                    {\lim_\to}_i Hom_{\mathcal{E}}(X, A_i)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{f_*}
                    \\\
                    * &amp;\stackrel{Id_x}{\to}&amp; Hom_{\mathcal{E}}(X,X)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              By
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+colimits"} universal colimits
              in the topos
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℰ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Id
                      %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℰ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Id
                      %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                      %mi i
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma({\lim_\to}_i (A_i \to X)))
                    \\simeq
                    Hom_{\mathcal{E}/X}(Id_X, {\lim_\to}_i (A_i \to X))
                    \\simeq
                    {\lim_\to}_i Hom_{\mathcal{E}/X}(Id_X,(A_i \to X))
                    \\simeq
                    {\lim_\to}_i \Gamma(A_i \to X)
                    \\,.
            %p
              So
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              does commute with colimits if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is tiny. By the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor+theorem"} adjoint functor theorem
              then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∇
                    %mo :
                    %mi Set
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla : Set \to \mathcal{E}/X
              does exist and so
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}/X
              is a local topos.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_6 Remark
            %p
              As a special case this reproduces the
              %a{:href => "#LocalizationOfPresheafTopos"} above statement
              that slices
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C)/j(U)
              of presheaf toposes over objects in the image of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
              are local: every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable functor
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tiny+object"} tiny
              (see there).
          %h3#gros_toposes Gros toposes
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            (such as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            or a
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec A
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+spectrum"} prime spectrum
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒵
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{Z}_A
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/big+and+little+toposes"} big
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zariski+site"} Zariski topos
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            (i.e. the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+topos"} classifying topos
            for
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+ring"}
                local
                = succeed "-algebras" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi 𝔭
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi A
                    %mo :
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∉
                    %mi 𝔭
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D (a) = \{ \mathfrak{p} \in Spec A : a \notin \mathfrak{p} \}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec A
            spanned by these basic open subsets admits a contravariant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full embedding
            in the category of finitely-presented
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi A
